    against it per scenario (in scenario order): ``count`` is the item's
    ``count`` minus the reference's; ``states`` is a list of three count
    differences ordered ``stable, uncertain, divergent``; when both
    rows' ``interval`` is present, ``interval`` is
    ``[item.lo − reference.lo, item.hi − reference.hi]`` and otherwise
    ``None``; ``from`` and ``to`` take the reference's and the item's
    ``state`` respectively (either may be ``None``); when both rows'
    ``rank`` is present, ``rank`` is the item's rank minus the
    reference's and otherwise ``None``.

